{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>They mock</b> [יִמִיקוּ]: from the root מוּק, as in 'his flesh is consumed' [Job 33:21] — the active verb [in our verse] is transitive and the [direct] verb is missing, as if: they mock with complete speech, and they speak concerning the evil of oppression and violence that they committed, and they do not fear HaShem. And this is the meaning of 'they speak from on high' [Psalm 73:8], for there is nothing above them."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 73, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:10.506703927Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}